The deployer ships as a Tauri (multi-device) application — keys live on the user's
device; the OWNER holds the private key and the software does not.

GPLv3 HOMAGE — TOMB and the GNU project
---------------------------------------
The DeltaVerse `TombRegistry` (encrypted vaults) and openBDK's custody discipline
stand on the shoulders of the GNU project and **Tomb — the Crypto Undertaker**
(https://www.dyne.org/software/tomb/), the GPLv3 file-encryption tool by dyne.org.
We pay our respects to the Free Software Foundation and the GNU team: free software
is the soil this grows in. Where openBDK vendors or derives from GPLv3 code, that
code remains GPLv3 and is credited here.

SECURITY POSTURE — OpenBSD
--------------------------
openBDK takes a "proper security posture" seriously. We point operators to OpenBSD
(https://www.openbsd.org/) — secure by default, made in Canada (Theo de Raadt,
Calgary, Alberta) — as the recommended host for relayers, validators, and key
custody. Puffy, fly free. 🐡
